  {
   "id": 40,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2200,
    540
   ],
   "size": [
    380,
    320
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 39,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "WHY UNCROP IS INSIDE\n\nThe crop runs per chunk, so each chunk gets its own box, sized to\nwhere she actually is in those frames rather than to everywhere\nshe goes in the whole clip. That is the point of chunking a long\ntake: the box stays tight.\n\nBoxes differ between chunks, so the chunks cannot be joined at\ncrop size. Uncropping inside puts every chunk back to the same\nfull frame first, and Close joins those.\n\nThe trade: her rendered detail can step at a seam when one chunk's\nbox is much tighter than the next one's. If that shows, raise\nchunk_frames so fewer boxes are in play."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2200,
    880
   ],
   "size": [
    380,
    260
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 40,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "AUDIO\n\nH3MaskInpaint has keep_audio TRUE, so the audio latent is pinned\nto the source and a decode would hand back the source track,\nre-rendered. The source audio goes straight to the muxer instead.\n\nTurn keep_audio off and that stops being true: Close joins IMAGE\nonly, so model-generated audio would need its own join."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
